/-!
# Every block of `ret0.w`'s AArch64 code at its place

Generated by `scc --code`. `ret0Prog` and `ret0Secs` are the program and
the data sections the canonical loader reads from the listing `ret0Asm`
(`Scc.Sem.A64.textProgram`, `Scc.Sem.dataSections`, at elaboration time); the
kernel cannot run the parsers, so these two equations are the trust boundary,
checked by evaluation (`#guard`).

Per function, the table of its `block_spec` blocks (`scc --blocks`, named in
comments), grouped by the label before them with their instruction counts
from it, in program order; `ret0T_in` checks them all against `ret0Prog` by
`kernel_rfl` (`blocksIn`, `Scc/Cert/Rt/CodeA64.lean`): every block is code
at its label and offset in every layout of the program
(`codeAt_of_blocksIn`), the loaded thread's included (`lays_threadAt`).

`ret0Λ` is the layout of the program's static link (`Scc.Cert.Link`),
with the program's immediate table `ret0Imms` when stated (`Layout.imms`):
`ret0Λ_wf` its well-formedness, `ret0Λ_aborts` its abort labels in the
program, `ret0Λ_image` each data symbol's item in its image
(`Scc.Cert.Link.image_symbols`), `ret0Λ_load` the canonical loader's checks
of it (but the entry state's), with a valid layout of the loaded thread
(`validLayout_of_loadOk`). `ret0_wide`, if stated, puts the program in the
one-word fragment (`Scc.Cert.WideA64.wideIn`), so its certification
semantics writes words only (`wideSt_threadAt`). `ret0_abort` checks the
abort stubs and `scc_rt_abort`, `ret0_print` `scc_rt_print`
(`Scc/Cert/Rt/A64Print.lean`), and `ret0_mainTail`, when stated (the
listing has it in a shape Spike proves), the tail of `scc_rt_main`: the
code the runtime's proofs take as hypotheses (`Scc/Cert/Rt/A64Abort.lean`);
`ret0_printL`, when stated, `wc_printL`'s (`Scc/Cert/Rt/A64PrintL.lean`).
`ret0Need`, if stated, is
the stack need of its stack-checked functions, checked on `ret0Prog`
(`ret0Need_ok`, `Scc/Cert/NeedA64.lean`).
-/

